### name: stmt.text-identity.schema-collation.sqlite
--- dialect
sqlite
--- options
{"strict":true}
--- bindings
{"R":{"kind":"relation","from":"r","fields":{"CAT":{"kind":"column","column":"cat","type":"TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> BUCKET(_["cat"], RECORD("cat", _K, "n", COUNT(_)))
--- expect
SELECT CAST("cat" AS TEXT) COLLATE BINARY AS "cat", COUNT(*) AS "n" FROM "r" GROUP BY CAST("cat" AS TEXT) COLLATE BINARY
--- note
Explicit BINARY overrides both NOCASE and RTRIM declarations, which survive CAST.
===

### name: stmt.text-identity.schema-distinct.sqlite
--- dialect
sqlite
--- options
{"strict":true}
--- bindings
{"R":{"kind":"relation","from":"r","fields":{"CAT":{"kind":"column","column":"cat","type":"TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("cat", _["cat"])) .> DISTINCT()
--- expect
SELECT DISTINCT CAST("cat" AS TEXT) COLLATE BINARY AS "cat" FROM "r"
===
